./services/platform/backend/MIGRATION.md:92:| Frontend data layer (hint hook + auth client + api client)      | done                     | inc 17: `app/lib/backend/` — fetch client (base path + org scope + `BackendApiError` normalization), `['backend', orgId, entity]` query-key vocabulary bound to the outbox's entity names, and `useBackendHints` (`/events` EventSource → `invalidateQueries` by entity prefix); dev proxy: `TALE_BACKEND_URL` routes `/api/auth` + `/api/app` + `/events` to the pg backend while everything else keeps flowing to Convex (proven end-to-end through Vite: sign-up cookie → session → /api/app → /events 403 → non-migrated /api falls through). Auth client unchanged (already talks to `/api/auth`; the convex-token plugin dies with the WS provider at shell migration). inc 72: the FIRST migrated vertical — the ACCOUNT BOOTSTRAP (dashboard gate): `app/lib/backend/account.ts` (queryOptions for `GET /two-factor/status` + `GET /users/password-expiry`, keyed `['backend','me','account',…]` — user-scoped, no hint lane; retry transport-only, a 4xx is a deterministic answer) consumed by `AccountBootstrapProvider`, the context's off-dashboard fallbacks, and the `/dashboard` loader prefetches; the `useConvexAuth().isAuthenticated` gating DROPPED for these reads (the session cookie is the auth — the 2FA overlay now lifts without waiting for the WS handshake; type identity kept by importing the 0.4 validator-derived types type-only). VERIFIED in a real browser (vite + `TALE_BACKEND_URL` + the pg backend): loader prefetches hit the backend (200/200), the gate overlay lifts on `decision:'ok'`, wire shapes exact. FOUND EN ROUTE: `npx convex dev --once` NO LONGER BUNDLES on branch 0.5 (esbuild: `node:fs/promises`/`node:path` unresolved via `convex/lib/file_io.ts` + `convex/governance/file_utils.ts` — some hoist added a V8→'use node' import edge), so the hybrid dev posture's Convex half cannot boot from this worktree; the browser run used a WS acceptor stub on :3210 to keep the OnlineGate (pure `isWebSocketConnected`) lifted. inc 73 REPAIRED the convex-dev bundling: the ROOT CAUSE was inc 59's `enterprise_sso/config/file_store.ts` hoist missing its `'use node'` pragma — the Convex CLI bundles EVERY file under convex/ as an entry point partitioned by that file's OWN pragma (importers are irrelevant), so one pragma-less file with `node:*` imports breaks the whole V8 bundle. One pragma restored the full hybrid loop (fleet READY in 92s: convex push green, auth routes probe green through the proxy, the auth pages render on live Convex queries; sso suites 75/75). Known hybrid split-brain until the users vertical migrates: `hasAnyUsers` reads CONVEX (empty — auth lives on pg) so a signed-out visit routes to /setup. inc 74: the SESSION/ORG BOOTSTRAP vertical — the whole boot chain off pg: `app/lib/backend/account.ts` grew hasAnyUsers/currentUser/account-flags; new `app/lib/backend/org.ts` (user-organizations listing, organization detail projected onto the 0.4 document shape, member context + my-teams typed VERBATIM off the 0.4 queries (type-only imports — re-declaring drifted on day one), last-active pointer, `recordOrgSwitch`, the public SSO discovery pair). Backend growth: `GET /api/app/organizations` (memberships listing, disabled excluded, role normalized), `GET /api/app/teams/mine` (the getMyTeams shape), and the PUBLIC `GET /api/app/sso/discovery/{configured,selectable}` (the 0.4 pre-auth login-page pair, mounted BEFORE the admin family's session gate; `listSelectableSsoConnections`/`getSsoDiscoveryStatus` walk the org files, cap 20). Swapped consumers: the auth-page hooks (hasAny/SSO discovery/account flags), `useAuth`'s identity probe (`/users/me` — 401 = signed out, no WS), `useCurrentMemberContext`, the org hooks, the dashboard index resolver (org list + last-active + switch), `/dashboard/$id` (loader preloads member context + my-teams over the backend; the persisted-role hydration + skip flags now read the SESSION PROBE via `useAuth`, not `useConvexAuth` — THE lesson of this increment: a boot-path surface gating on WS auth dead-loops once its data moves to HTTP; `create-organization` kicked every visitor back to /log-in until its auth source moved to the probe), the org-switch sweep (drops `['backend', <old-org>, …]` keys alongside the convex ones, `me` rows kept), settings account/organization loaders, forced-change-password, the 2FA enroll page + settings 2FA/passkey sections (status → HTTP with explicit invalidation at every flip: enroll verify, disable, passkey register/revoke). Integration 142/142 (+ user-organizations listing probe, sso discovery on/off probes in the admin check). BROWSER-verified on the hybrid fleet: login form renders off pg hasAnyUsers (the /setup split-brain is GONE), sign-in → resolver → onboarding wizard → org created → `recordOrgSwitch` → the FULL dashboard shell (role-gated nav rail from the pg member context) with the Convex WS never authenticating. inc 75: the HINT LANE live — `useBackendHints(organizationId)` mounted in the `$id` layout (one org-scoped EventSource for the whole shell; invalidates `['backend', orgId, entity]` by prefix), and the bootstrap entities' writers now EMIT: `member` hints on add/role-change/remove (in the same tx as the write + audit) and `team` hints on team-member add/remove — the shell's member context and team filter refresh live again (the 0.4 WS-reactivity parity for the migrated reads). The `me`-scoped rows (memberships list, account reads) stay refetch-only by design — no org stream addresses them. Organization-rename hints ride the settings vertical (the write lives on Better Auth's own endpoint). Integration 142/142 (teams check grew /teams/mine + team-hint 1→2 + the member add→role→remove 3-hint lifecycle probes); full UI suite 3443/3443. inc 76: the CHAT THREAD FAMILY — the first feature vertical, and the pattern every family follows: (1) the seam's engine (`useChatQuery`) grew an HTTP LANE — a name-keyed adapter table (`HTTP_READS`, keyed by the same 0.4 function names the watches key on: the client-side twin of the backend's ctx shim) routes a MIGRATED family's reads through react-query (`keepPreviousData` + the org hint stream) while every other read keeps its Convex watch, hook order stable, session-cache semantics shared, provider-less renders served by a module fallback client (`useChatQueryClient` — the action hooks invalidate through the same client the reads populate); (2) `app/lib/backend/chat.ts` — the thread family's options + writes (list/archived/summary(404→null)/branches/search reads projecting null→optional ONCE; create + 15 verb writes); (3) the route layer emits USER-TARGETED `chat_thread` hints after every successful thread write (create/capabilities/effort/move/rename/pin/read/archive/share-project/share/unshare/branch×3/branch-selection/trash/restore — one `hintThread` helper), so another tab's write invalidates by prefix; (4) reads AND writes swap TOGETHER per family — a split leaves hybrid dev with two stores disagreeing (the lesson that shaped the slicing); thread-actions/thread-sharing/branch-actions(thread half)/move/effort hooks now fetch pg and nudge the family prefix locally. The `useChatSend` thread CREATES stay with the turn family — the created thread is immediately sent into, and the send still runs on Convex until inc 77. Integration 142/142; full UI suite green (the seam's watch-stability invariants re-pointed at a still-WS read + an HTTP-lane stability twin: ONE fetch, steady `ready`). Hybrid browser: create-thread 201 → the chat index auto-opened the newest PG thread (the sidebar list consumed the backend); the thread PAGE still error-boundaries on the UNMIGRATED deferred-sends read (`usePaginatedQuery` throws UNAUTHENTICATED on the dead WS) — inc 77's family removes it, and full sidebar-interaction verification rides that. inc 77: the TURN FAMILY — the chat surface's live core off pg: (1) messages joined `HTTP_READS` (the rows already ship the view shape; the GET's gate widened to owner-OR-project-shared — the 0.4 `listMessages` posture the inc-16 route had narrowed); (2) the LIVE lane is a per-thread SSE STORE (`thread-stream.ts`: one EventSource per (org, thread) with subscriber counting over `GET /threads/:id/stream`; the route now emits an IMMEDIATE `idle` so an idle thread resolves instantly instead of a heartbeat later, and `progress` grew `serverNow` for the thinking timer's clock offset) feeding BOTH `useChatGeneration` (status view) and the new `useChatGenerationText` — `useThreadView` consumes them, and a `settled` event invalidates messages + threads so the transcript swaps to durable rows even if a beat was missed; (3) `useChatSend` fully HTTP: create → video bind (`/video-links/bind`) → `POST /messages` (resolves at settle — the 0.4 action contract; refusals arrive AS DATA on non-2xx so the send uses a raw fetch, the shared client would flatten the reason) + stop → `/cancel` + defer → `/deferred-sends` + unbind; (4) the DEFERRED-SEND VIDEO CLAIM landed (the ledgered `bind_for_send` gap): `deferred_sends.video_job_ids` (the column 0025 ALREADY SHIPPED forward-looking — the near-miss: a duplicate migration failed the concurrent-boot race and the diagnosis walked the whole advisory-lock chain before grep found 0025's `text[]`), enqueue claims via `bindJobsForDeferredSend` (stamp releases the composer chips), readiness grew the real video leg (terminal-or-handoff-settled releases; a vanished row reads erased-proceed), the poll's fire builds `buildBoundJobAttachments` (video/mp4 sentinel; not-ready excluded), cancel cascades `cancelDeferredJobs` (unbind-in-the-same-update + skip + Whisper early-exit + cleanup); (5) the TRAY reads/actions over HTTP (rows typed `DeferredSendView`/`VideoLinkJobView`); (6) regenerate = the send door with `resend: true` (the 0.4 `regenerateTurn` IS `startTurn`+resend — no new route); (7) the COMPOSER MODELS read swapped to `GET /composer/models` (it gates the send affordance, so it ships with this family; the rest of the composer lane — capabilities menus — waits). Integration 142/142 (run 137); chat UI suite 381/381 (the seam's invariant tests re-pointed at the still-WS questions read + a FakeEventSource stream test + fetch-driven send tests). BROWSER end-to-end on the hybrid fleet with a scripted STREAMING fake provider (org custom provider + credential — catalog entries need `context_length` or the normalizer drops them): the thread page renders (the tray crash is gone), the picker lists the pg catalog, send → live status + ticking thinking timer (SSE-driven) → settled reply in the transcript → a SECOND turn reuses the same stream. inc 78: the CHAT SATELLITES — everything else the chat feature read or wrote over the websocket, swapped in one sweep: FEEDBACK (a new thread-scoped my-ratings route `GET /feedback/thread/:threadId` + submit/remove — the toolbar's latch), the VOICE family (voice-mode adapter row; `useVoiceChunks` polls `GET /tts/messages/:id/chunks` at 1s with the org threaded down through the player/indicator; synthesize/dictation/thread-override/user-default over their routes; a NEW `GET /tts/messages/:id/usage` aggregate serves the info dialog's per-message voice spend — `getMessageVoiceUsage` finally ported), FILE STATUSES (a new `POST /files/statuses` batch read in the 0.4 `getByStorageIds` shape — first row per ref, cap 20; the two staging hooks poll at 2s, source-cards rides a non-polling adapter row), VIDEO CHIPS (`use-chat-video-links` reads poll the thread/unbound routes; ingest drops the client-derived dedup fields — the 0.5 route normalizes server-side; refusal codes now read `BackendApiError.code` alongside ConvexError data), the SHARED-THREAD snapshot view, PREFERENCES (my-preferences adapter row + the sticky chat-model save), the chat sub-panel's PROJECT folders (list adapter row + pin), LEGAL-HOLD badges (a new member-readable `GET /legal-holds/targets?targetType=` — org flag + direct + custodian-cascade ids, mirroring the 0.4 round-2 P0 posture), the BUDGET banner's request-credits door (`POST /organizations/:id/request-credits` → one system bell via `writeNotificationForOrgs`), and the PERCEIVED-WAIT metric (`POST /chat/messages/:id/perceived-wait` — usage-blob merge, fire-once, owner+assistant-only in one UPDATE…FROM). Every response typed off the 0.4 validators (`FunctionReturnType`, the drift-proof rule); every chat-feature direct read passes the seam's context-or-fallback client so provider-less renders keep working — and the surface TEST file re-pins its everything-unavailable default (the HTTP lane now WORKS provider-less, which un-degraded renders the old calibration relied on). The chat feature's remaining websocket surface: questions + arena, both unbuilt server-side. Integration 142/142; chat suite 381/381; full UI suite 3444/3444. inc 79: the PROJECTS VERTICAL — and the seam every remaining vertical rides: the app-wide Convex hook WRAPPERS (`useConvexQuery`/`useConvexMutation`/`useConvexAction`/`useActionQuery`) grew a name-keyed HTTP adapter registry (`app/lib/backend/convex-adapters.ts` — `READ_ADAPTERS`/`WRITE_ADAPTERS`/`ACTION_QUERY_ADAPTERS`, keys = `getFunctionName`), so a family swaps reads AND writes by contributing rows while ~150 call sites keep compiling untouched; adapted reads drop the WS-auth gate (session cookie IS the auth), adapted writes invalidate through the ambient query client BEFORE the caller's onSuccess, optimistic updates are ignored on the HTTP lane (no Convex store to patch), and every deterministic 4xx is rethrown as a REAL `ConvexError` carrying `{code, message, ...data}` (`BackendApiError` grew `data` so `PROJECT_HAS_BOUND_AUTOMATIONS` still names the automations in the delete dialog; 5xx stays transport = retryable). The fallback org for rows whose 0.4 args omit `organizationId` comes from `activeOrganizationId()` — a PURE URL read (`/dashboard/$id/…`, base path stripped), because the wrappers also render ABOVE the RouterProvider (BrandingProvider) where a router hook throws and white-screens the app (found live). `app/lib/backend/projects.ts` carries the family: reads list/overview(+asOf)/detail(404-or-403→null — the 0.4 answer)/agents/sidebar/search + the palette search twin (client-side `key · description` snippet, capped 600), project chats (keyed under `chat_thread` so thread hints refresh the tab), agent-secrets listing, and the two composer walks (models + project capabilities) as action-query rows; writes create/7×settings/pin/archive/restore/duplicate/delete(+counts)/agents CRUD/secrets upsert+delete/thread move+share (reusing chat.ts verbs — no second copies); the projects route loader prefetches through the SAME exported options builder the adapter row uses (`projectsOverviewQuery`), replacing the dead convex prefetch. FOUND EN ROUTE and fixed: every post-auth-change invalidation still targeted only `['auth','session']` while `useAuth` reads `['backend','me','account','current-user']` — a cached signed-out (or previous-identity) answer survived sign-up/log-in/2FA until a lucky remount; `invalidateAuthState` (session-query.ts) now drops BOTH scopes at all 11 identity/membership-changing sites (the setup wizard's Next stayed disabled forever without it — caught in the browser). NOT adapted by design: project files/folders reads + detach + the files-tab write trio (the DOCUMENTS family — its pg projection still lacks ragStatus/record). inc 80 closed the two backend gaps: project secrets (the Environment tab's read + set/pair/delete rows — browser-proven write→encrypted-at-rest→masked listing round trip) and the two serving previews (action-query rows onto the lane routes). inc 81: the TASKS BOARD CORE rides the same registry — `app/lib/backend/tasks.ts` (9 reads incl. the all-projects board, 19 writes; `projects/queries:listAccessibleUserIds` row serves the actor directory); board/list/detail/discussion/subtasks/dependencies/activity/labels all HTTP, BROWSER-proven: create AP-1 → card on the board with the project-key number → comment → status picker moves the card between columns with the comment chip counting (write→invalidate→refetch loop live). Integration 143/143 (run 141: flags + real-overdue + detach-walk-releases-the-thread + secrets-gate probes); full UI suite 3452/3452; wrapper/adapter/row unit tests added. BROWSER on the hybrid fleet (fresh install): setup wizard → org → projects list/overview table (rollups, Org-wide flag) → create → General rename+instructions saved live into the breadcrumb → Chats tab + the chat panel showing the rename (cross-family hint invalidation) → Agents tab dialog with all three catalogs resolving (needs `TALE_CONFIG_DIR` — the ported config readers throw without it) → palette search with the 0.4 snippet → duplicate ' (copy)' → detach delete. inc 119: the seam AUDIT — every `api.*` reference the app reaches for, checked against the registries. Seven call sites were still holding raw `convex/react` hooks, so they would have kept the dead WS lane after cutover no matter what the registry said: the builder-session start, the changelog feed, the attachment pipeline-status read (chat had a row; tasks and conversations render the SAME component and did not), the automation settings panel's read AND write, onboarding completion, org-deletion cleanup, and the changelog dot/toast state. All seven now ride the wrappers, with their rows added (`accountReadAdapters`/`accountWriteAdapters`/`accountActionQueryAdapters`, `orgWriteAdapters`, the documents action-query pair, the file-status read, the prefs and builder writes). FOUND EN ROUTE: the settings panel's file pair had NO 0.5 door at all — `backend/domains/documents/project-text.ts` ports it (folder resolved on demand, blob written before any row so a failed store cannot leave a dangling ref, upsert keyed by `external_item_id` so a re-save rewrites in place instead of forking, `skipRagIndexing` because a settings file is not knowledge, absence in every form reads as `{}` so a first-run form falls back to its declared defaults, and a file NAME may not contain a path). inc 120: the CONTACTS and PRODUCTS verticals cut over — their paginated lanes were adapted in inc 96, but every other row still rode the WS: the whole-list reads (the conversation composer's contact lookup), the table headers' counts, the palette search, and all of CRUD + CSV import. Three doors were MISSING on 0.5 and are now built: `/contacts/count` + `/products/count` (an exact count, the 0.5 idiom, replacing 0.4's walk-to-a-cap-of-20 probe), `/contacts/bulk` + `/products/bulk` (the import lane — `bulkCreateContacts` had a service but no route, `bulkCreateProducts` had neither; each row runs in its OWN transaction so a refused one never aborts the import, and the caller gets the per-row account 0.4 returned), and `/contacts/search` (the ⌘K palette: name/email/external-id, the 0.4 snippet assembled the same way, an empty term listing NOTHING rather than the org). inc 121: KNOWLEDGE ENTRIES and WEBSITES cut over (counts, version chains, the whole-site listing, all of CRUD, and the crawler dialogs' pages/chunks/search — the last three call their reads AS actions, the 0.4 shape, so they ride the write lane). And the LOADER lane, which no audit had covered: ten route loaders still prefetched through `convexQuery(...)`, which after cutover would fire a doomed WebSocket query AND warm a key the component no longer reads — the prefetch's whole purpose (painting without a skeleton flash) silently lost. `lib/backend/prefetch.ts` adds `prefetchAdaptedQuery` / `ensureAdaptedQueryData`: same lane the component will use, same key, with the Convex path kept for rows that have no adapter yet. inc 122: the INBOX cut over — the whole-list read, the per-status counts, the conversation detail, and every write (five bulk verbs, close/reopen/spam, read, assign to a person or a team, delete, reply, compose, undo/retry/discard, attachments). FOUND EN ROUTE, and the reason this row could not have been closed by wiring alone: the pg row and the 0.4 Inbox item are DIFFERENT SHAPES — the UI reads a conversation one level deep (`title`, `description`, `message_count`, `contact`, `messages`), and the adapted paginated lane had been handing it the raw row, so titles and previews would have rendered blank. `lib/shared/conversations/conversation-item.ts` now owns that projection for BOTH lanes (0.4's `transformConversation` rewired onto it, its 263 tests green), the 0.5 list and detail doors answer with it (a list row carries only the newest message — all a preview needs — the detail carries the thread), and the integration probe asserts the shape on both. Two 0.4 lanes that are OFFLINE stay offline, deliberately: `downloadAttachments` (0.4's action is a no-op) becomes the guards alone — the message must be visible and its conversation must carry a connector, so an unstamped conversation fails CLOSED instead of dispatching through whichever provider is configured — and `improveMessage` answers with 0.4's own graceful-degrade contract rather than leaving the button on a lane that will not exist after cutover. inc 123 closes the seam: a second full audit of every `api.*` reference the app reaches for leaves NOTHING shipped on the WebSocket. Wired: the approvals decide door, project detach, the file-url read (single and a NEW batch door — the attachment lists ask for many, and the 0.4 lane's own comment warns that a cap here silently drops thumbnails, so it never truncates and an unresolvable ref answers `url: null` instead of failing the batch), the three transcription/registration writes, the folder breadcrumb, and two surfaces that had no 0.5 door at all: the security page's sign-in BLOCK COUNTERS (counters are keyed by email, so the org scope is this org's member emails — another tenant's security event must never surface) and the run dialog's EXECUTION LOG (`getAgentNodeSandboxOp`, keyed by the run's derived session id; it polls on the